WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:02.302
He's back or is he?

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.404
Welcome to Unfiltered. I'm S.E. Cupp.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.540
The Donald Trump of 2016

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.844
who slayed more than a dozen GOP dragons

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.479
in the Republican primary

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:13.446
to become

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.749
the unlikely nominee for president

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.984
is hoping to make a comeback.

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:21.521
Looking for a repeat of 2016 In 2024

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:22.756
Trump appears

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:24.958
to be reverting to the old playbook,

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:27.460
swinging hard and early at his opponents.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:30.330
We all remember the ugly punches

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.164
he threw,

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.033
many of which were unprecedented

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.667
in their nastiness,

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.903
trashing Carly Fiorina's face,

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.505
attacking Ted Cruz's

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:39.439
wife,

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:42.108
mocking little Marco Rubio's stature.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:44.878
Questioning Ben Carson's faith,

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.913
Groh says it was it worked.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.382
No one was able to match him in the ring.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.216
His voters

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.051
seemed to revel

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:51.751
in the name calling,

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:54.387
while the rest of us cringed.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.322
He'd carry the act into his presidency,

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.690
lashing out at opponents

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.659
both real and imaginary.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.728
Getting in the gutter whenever possible.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.531
Trump's act was novel back then.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.066
But what about now?

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.301
More than six years later,

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:11.271
we've seen this show thousands of times

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:14.174
at rallies, on Twitter and truth social,

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.643
in interviews and on debate stages.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.412
It isn't titillating or shocking now.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.481
It's almost boring, in fact.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.550
And his punches seem to have lost

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.452
some of their sting.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.519
Back in November, Trump

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.720
tried out a new nickname

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.922
for Florida Governor

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.256
Ron DeSantis,

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.558
who is believed to be

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.493
considering a run for president.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:36.463
Calling him Ron just sanctimonious.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.997
At a Pennsylvania rally

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.567
sounding a little more

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.968
erudite than Trump's

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.036
usual schoolyard

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:45.405
taunts, the nickname hasn't stuck.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:46.739
This week,

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.476
he called DeSantis a rhino globalist

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.044
for pushing vaccines

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:53.146
and COVID testing in Florida.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.581
Somehow that doesn't seem

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.449
all that fatal either.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.317
Trump's insisting

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.786
that DeSantis would be very disloyal

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.087
if you challenged him.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.956
But a number of GOP

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.992
senators, from John Cornyn to John Thune,

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:07.494
Cynthia Lummis to Marco

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:09.529
Rubio have said no.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.898
Anyone can run.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.867
Former U.S. ambassador to the U.N.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:14.968
Nikki Haley,

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:15.902
a onetime Trump

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.971
supporter, is also expected

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.772
to throw her hat in the ring.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.008
Thus far, Trump had a light touch,

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.209
questioning her honor

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.244
while encouraging her

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:26.513
to try taking him on.

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.014
And he mocked his former vice

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.215
president, Mike Pence,

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.050
who is also mulling a run

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.952
for coming in at 7%

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.088
in a poll of hypothetical GOP

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:36.890
presidential contenders.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.058
Oh, Mike is doing better than I thought.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.461
He poked Mitt.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:41.861
Sorry.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:42.128
I know

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.029
we're just getting started,

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.397
but this Trump doesn't

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.598
seem to pack the punch

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.600
that 2016 Trump did

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.669
His fundraising numbers appear to agree.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.372
He's brought in $9.5 million

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.540
in the six weeks

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.108
since he announced his bid

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:57.076
compared to the 11.8 million

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.245
he raised before the announcement.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.281
Going in the wrong direction.

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.883
It's early but so far this Trump seems.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.753
How should we say low energy.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:07.887
Maybe he's lost his touch

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:08.221
as he's

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.990
faced one political storm after another.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.992
Or maybe we've just been to see

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:13.860
the wizard

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.895
and we've seen behind the curtain.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.665
And he isn't all that impressive anymore.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.800
Only time will tell as more and more

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.703
Republicans get in the race and test

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.638
whether the Trump punch

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.740
has lost its sting.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.642
That's it for me. See you next week.

